I'm playing the Valkyrie, since I've given up with the other characters. It
take's far too long to get a half decent character going (i.e. one which
survives the mines). That makes the game really boring, I strongly suggest
that the dev team reconsider the other characters starting abilities.
It's incredible just how easy it is to get Mjollnir. A couple of dead bodies
on the altar and Odin's given you the next best thing to a wand of death.

I've now finished the quest. That was a real joke:
I find Lord Sutur's den, he stands one space behind me hurling verbal abuse
and a stone gaint starts zapping a wand of death at me from the other side.
4 Zaps miss me and the 5th Zap goes staight passed me and wacks Sutur.  I
wack the gaint and the quest is over. I never even laid a finger on him.
Bizarre! I don't know how often I've seen a good character of mine die due
to plain bad luck (and the obituary intrinsics said "you where extremely
lucky", oh yeah?), it's really nice to get some wild good luck in your
characters favour for a change.

Anyway I mucked the game up later on, by accidently droping my bag on a
"polypile" heap, and polypiling it. Is there anyway to get the bag or
contents back? I had a few good artifact weapons, wands scrolls, etc..
Also, I've got V3.1.1 running, when I get the wand of wishing is there any
point in asking for the PYEC, or would that be a waste of a wish. I've seen
a few people saying in this newsgroup that it's almost impossible to get
even if you are a neutral character.

And finally what's the best way to get enchant armor scrolls with a wand of
wishing? I'd like to get as many a possible for Rust&Fire protection as well
as hit points. Asking for a blessed magic marker and recharging it, or
asking just for the scrolls themselves? I've noticed that reading blessed
scrolls of enchant armor while confused doesn't fire or rust protect your
armor. Why?

My grumbles are only minor, it's a brilliant piece of work dev team!

George

